<title>JAPAN: Kawasaki Steel rises on bargain-hunting.</title>
<headline>Kawasaki Steel rises on bargain-hunting.</headline>
<dateline>TOKYO 1997-04-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Kawasaki Steel shares rose in early Friday morning trade as investors continued to hunt for relatively low-priced issues backed by solid earnings, brokers said.</p>
<p>As of 0034 GMT, the shares were two yen higher at 366, matching the new high for the calendar year set on Thursday. Turnover totalled 6.83 million shares, making it the most heavily traded issue on the first section of the Tokyo bourse.</p>
</text>
